\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits record low, euro warning shrugged off.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 13:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The dollar tumbled to a record low against the euro on Tuesday after a warning by euro zone officials on the euro's rise fell on deaf ears, with investors determined to dump the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In a joint statement late on Monday, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro zone finance ministers gave their starkest warning to date that they were unhappy with the euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 In an echo of developments that preceded the ECB's maiden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets of 2000, the statement said policymakers were monitoring the situation closely.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar, under pressure from concerns about the wide U.S.\par current account deficit, hit a low around $1.3470 per euro  and a\par 12-year low versus sterling beyond $1.95       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The credibility of the threat of ECB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is low particularly after the ECB discussed an interest rate hike last week. It makes no sense to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and raise rates at the same time," said Carsten Fritsch, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Commerzbank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Unless action is taken at this stage the dollar will fall further."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said a report in the Wall Street Journal Europe questioning the U.S. government's triple-A bond rating also hurt the greenback.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The WSJE article, which canvassed investors' opinions on the U.S.' rating, triggered selling in a market already prepared to take the dollar lower.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A U.S. ratings downgrade may not be imminent but it's food for thought," said Paul Mackel, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Should it happen, it could jeopardise the benchmark status of Treasuries and make it even harder for the U.S. to finance its current account deficit."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By 1230 GMT, the dollar was down around half a percent on the day at $1.3453 per euro and 102.70 yen. It has shed roughly nine percent against the euro and the yen in the past two months.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The closely-watched German ZEW expectations indicator rose unexpectedly to 14.4 in December from 13.9 in November as a drop in crude oil costs helped offset concern about the impact of the rising euro on the key export sector.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EURO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar initially bounced as the euro zone finance ministers' statement late on Monday fuelled jitters over potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the effect was short-lived, particularly as the ECB surprised financial markets last week by revealing it had considered raising interest rates even as the soaring euro was threatening to hit exports and growth prospects worsened.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the meantime, euro zone politicians kept up pressure on the United States to act on dollar weakness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Belgian finance minister Didier Reynders said on Tuesday that the statement was a clear message to the United States and it was up to the United States to do something about the imbalances in its economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Austrian finance minister Karl-Heinz Grasser said the United States must act, not just talk, to reduce an excessively high euro/dollar exchange rate by reducing its twin deficits.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREAT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were taking more seriously the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Japanese authorities, which spent around $330 billion trying to fight the dollar's slide between January 2003 and March 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated on Tuesday recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves were rapid and unwelcome.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest data from Japan on the October leading indicator suggested a possible economic downturn in the world's second largest economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  massively earlier this year so it's more credible regarding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . We also had disappointing data there, so \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to tolerate the dollar's weakness is lower than Europe," Fritsch said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Canada holds an interest rate meeting later and the Reserve Bank of Australia is also expected to publish a decision on rates. Both countries are expected to leave key rates unchanged.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041208e0c70051a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
