\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits record low, euro warning ignored.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The dollar tumbled to a record low against the euro on Tuesday after a warning by euro zone officials on the euro's rise fell on deaf ears, with investors determined to dump the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In a joint statement late on Monday, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro zone finance ministers gave their starkest warning to date that they were unhappy with the euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 In an echo of developments that preceded the ECB's maiden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets of 2000, the statement said policymakers were monitoring the situation closely.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar, under pressure from concerns about the massive U.S. current account deficit, hit a low around $1.3468 and a 12-year low against sterling beyond $1.95.  \par \par \uc2 "The credibility of the threat of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is low particularly after the ECB discussed an interest rate hike last week. It makes no sense to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and raise rates at the same time," said Carsten Fritsch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank.  \par \par \uc2 "Unless action is taken at this stage the dollar will fall further."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a report in the Wall Street Journal Europe questioning the U.S. government's triple-A bond rating also hurt the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 The WSJE article, which canvassed investors' opinions on the U.S.' rating, triggered selling in a market already prepared to take the dollar lower.  \par \par \uc2 A U.S. bank trader said: "I don't believe there will be a downgrade but the initial reaction was to sell the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 By 1030 GMT, the dollar stood at $1.3446 per euro, down a third of a percent from New York levels. It fetched 102.54 yen, down 0.6 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has shed roughly nine percent against the euro and the yen in the past two months.  \par \par \uc2 The closely-watched German ZEW expectations indicator rose unexpectedly to 14.4 in December from 13.9 in November as a drop in crude oil costs helped offset concern about the impact of the rising euro on the key export sector.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS?  \par \par \uc2 The dollar initially bounced as the euro zone finance ministers' statement late on Monday fuelled jitters over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 But the effect was short-lived, particularly as the ECB surprised financial markets last week by revealing it had considered raising interest rates even as the soaring euro was threatening to hit exports and growth prospects worsened.  \par \par \uc2 "The comments from the (euro group) meeting were largely repeating previous statements and they are not going to stem the current rise in the euro," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 In the meantime, euro zone politicians kept up pressure on the United States to act on the dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Belgian finance minister Didier Reynders said on Tuesday that the statement was a clear message to the United States and it was up to the United States to do something about the imbalances in its economy.  \par \par \uc2 Austrian finance minister Karl-Heinz Grasser said the United States must act, not just talk, to reduce an excessively high euro/dollar exchange rate by reducing its twin deficits.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT  \par \par \uc2 Investors were taking more seriously the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities, which spent around $330 billion trying to fight the dollar's slide between January 2003 and March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated earlier recent moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were rapid and unwelcome.  \par \par \uc2 The latest data from Japan on the October leading indicator suggested a possible economic downturn in the world's second largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively earlier this year so it's more credible regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We also had disappointing data there, so \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to tolerate the dollar's weakness is lower than Europe," Fritsch said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Canada holds an interest rate meeting later and the Reserve Bank of Australia is also expected to make a decision on rates public. Both countries are expected to leave key rates unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c7007so\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
