\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar edges up from lows, respite seen temporary.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Eric Burroughs  \par \uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 6 (Reuters) - The dollar clung to slim gains on Monday but stayed close to a record low against the euro and a five-year low vs the yen, with traders saying it was just a matter of time before the market dumps the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.   \par \par \uc2  A combination of profit-taking on bets against the dollar and worries about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the latest move lower, sparked by a surprisingly weak U.S. employment report on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials in particular have stepped up their warnings in recent days about taking dollar-buying action, calling recent market moves volatile and hinting at possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  But traders say the market will keep driving the dollar lower until \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurs. Some believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may ultimately act alone if yen strength accelerates.   \par \par \uc2  Since early October the yen has jumped nearly 9 percent against the dollar, while the euro has surged more than 9 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "While the ECB is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon, the yen's rise should be limited on wariness over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Yoshiyasu Naruse, head of corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at HSBC Ltd.   \par \par \uc2  A top policy maker in Japan's ruling party, Kaoru Yosano, told Reuters on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an option but was only effective in countering short-term, speculative moves.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled across the board on Friday after U.S. non-farm payrolls rose 112,000 in November, well below economists' median forecast for a rise of 180,000.   \par \par \uc2  While the data did not change the outlook for the Federal Reserve to steadily ratchet up official U.S. rates, it gave traders and investors yet another reason to sell the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  At 0655 GMT, the dollar was at around 102.25 yen, improving a tad from where it stood at the end of New York trade on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  In early Tokyo trade the dollar dipped to a low of 101.91 yen, slightly above a five-year low of 101.83 hit last week, before moving back up partly due to buying by Japanese importers, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly easier at $1.3430, versus $1.3454 in New York and a record high of $1.3461 marked on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  Sterling stood at around $1.9420 after matching a 12-year peak of $1.9442 earlier in the day.   \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar moved up to 1.1340 Swiss francs after hitting a nine-year low of 1.1301 in U.S. trade.   \par \par \uc2  RATES NOT A FACTOR   \par \par \uc2  The dollar has suffered incessant selling in the past two months on renewed worries about the giant U.S. trade and budget deficits and a widespread belief a weaker dollar is needed - and perhaps wanted by Washington - to correct them.   \par \par \uc2  The prospect of a higher U.S. Fed funds rate - which makes dollar deposits more attractive - has mattered little to markets.   \par \par \uc2  Despite the poor jobs data, a Reuters poll found that all 20 primary dealers surveyed expected the Fed to raise its key rate by a quarter percentage point to 2.25 percent at its December meeting. Sixteen of the 20 looked for another quarter-point tightening in February.   \par \par \uc2  "The interest rate outlook isn't a factor for the market," said Kikuko Takeda, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.   \par \par \uc2  "I think we should be prepared to see another round of dollar selling," she said, adding that the market would likely target a fall towards 100 yen and a rise in the euro to $1.35. (Additional reporting by Kazunori Takada).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c6004hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
