\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     PATRICK DYESS, TECHNICAL STRATEGIST, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CAPITAL\par MARKETS:\par     EURO/DOLLAR - "Fresh all-time highs were recorded at the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close of last week's session, falling just short of breaking  \f28 \par \par \uc2 the regression upper band. Neither a bid nor offer was dominant  \par \par \uc2 in the Asia and London sessions following the move into key  \par \par \uc2 resistance. The indication leaves us to deduce a period of  \par \par \uc2 consolidation is likely while the market catches its breath ...  \par \par \uc2 The former resistance, now support comes in at the previous all  \par \par \uc2 time high ($1.3360), with the $1.3300 figure (top of shoulder  \par \par \uc2 line) following that. Moves to these particular levels are  \par \par \uc2 likely to be snatched up by those attempting to establish a  \par \par \uc2 long bias after being forced into market neutral holdings.  \par \par \uc2 Resistance is rather close in proximity from present pricing,  \par \par \uc2 and we feel a test of the lower end of the range is more likely  \par \par \uc2 to come into play before a continuation of the trend."  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR/YEN - "The daily implies moves above last week's  \par \par \uc2 range are likely to be taken lower, as traders continue to test  \par \par \uc2 the resolve of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels down through  \par \par \uc2 parity. If clear \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes place, many traders are  \par \par \uc2 likely to adopt a strategy using a shorter time frame coupled  \par \par \uc2 with decisive moves in and out of the pair ... Going forward,  \par \par \uc2 we feel the recently influential 10-day simple moving average  \par \par \uc2 (102.80 yen) may act as an attractor, since it has done so in  \par \par \uc2 recent sessions. Following the 10-day simple moving average,  \par \par \uc2 last week's spike highs are probably going to contribute to  \par \par \uc2 resistance with a break opening up the gate to 104.35/50, as it  \par \par \uc2 coincides with the 23.6 percent of 111.60-102.15."  \par \par \uc2 STERLING/DOLLAR - "In no less than spectacular fashion,  \par \par \uc2 sterling yet again manages to make considerable gains on the  \par \par \uc2 benchmark, ending the week with a range of nearly 400-pips.  \par \par \uc2 Only one 24-hour period of last week's session lost ground  \par \par \uc2 against the dollar, but was promptly jettisoned following  \par \par \uc2 Friday's market events. The next level of resistance is  \par \par \uc2 difficult to gauge considering the pair has now forayed into  \par \par \uc2 fresh 12-year territory (or more appropriately unchartered  \par \par \uc2 territory). Key levels: Going forward, we remain cautious as  \par \par \uc2 key resistance levels have been frequently obliterated by this  \par \par \uc2 uncommonly one-sided price action. Thus, we have fallen back  \par \par \uc2 to the pivot and Fibonacci retracement levels for guidance as  \par \par \uc2 they have shifted momentously for the month of December. The  \par \par \uc2 monthly pivot comes in at the most recent break out near  \par \par \uc2 $1.8842. The pivot R1 comes in overhead at $1.9386 with the R2  \par \par \uc2 coming into play at $1.9675."  \par \par \uc2 THOMAS FITZPATRICK, CHIEF TECHNICAL ANALYST, CITIFX  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR/SWISS FRANC - "Now approaching the all-time lows on  \par \par \uc2 dollar/Swiss franc from April and October 1995, from 1.1221  \par \par \uc2 francs to 1.1120 francs. Although as would be expected Swiss  \par \par \uc2 franc appreciation is slowing ahead of these levels, with  \par \par \uc2 euro/Swiss franc and sterling/Swiss franc moving higher, the  \par \par \uc2 risk remains high for them to be testing eventually. Although  \par \par \uc2 as we've highlighted in intraday updates, it's definitely  \par \par \uc2 important to be cautious as we approach the all-time lows on a  \par \par \uc2 major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair such as dollar/Swiss franc."  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR INDEX - "As with dollar/Swiss franc, the U.S. dollar  \par \par \uc2 index now moving closer to the April 1995 lows at 80.05, below  \par \par \uc2 there the September 1992 lows at 74.93."  \par \par \uc2 EURO/YEN - "Euro/yen continues to push higher with the  \par \par \uc2 long-term consolidation resistance now nearing again. 138.25  \par \par \uc2 yen to 139.04 yen are the levels to watch. Above there would  \par \par \uc2 open things up."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 9:47 a.m. EST (1447 GMT). All data taken  \par \par \uc2 from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 in the previous New York session.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Last   US Close  %       YTD     2003\par                              03 Dec.   Change  %Change Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.3433   1.3453   -0.15   +6.73   1.2586\par Dlr/yen              102.42   102.06   +0.35   -4.57   107.33\par Euro/yen             137.63   137.33   +0.22   +1.91   135.05\par Dlr/swiss            1.1363   1.1304   +0.52   -8.37   1.2401\par Stg/dlr              1.9425   1.9433   -0.04   +8.81   1.7853\par Dlr/cad              1.2000   1.1902   +0.82   -7.46   1.2967\par Aus/dlr              0.7755   0.7816   -0.78   +3.18   0.7516\par Euro/swiss           1.5262   1.5212   +0.33   -2.17   1.5601\par Euro/stg             0.6915   0.6921   -0.09   -1.87   0.7047\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatilities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par  European markets......\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c600918\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
