\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar dangles precariously above recent lows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 13:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 6 (Reuters) - The dollar teetered above last week's record low against the euro and five-year low versus the yen on Monday as traders wondered for how long Europe and Japan would tolerate the greenback's slide.  \par \par \uc2 Sabre-rattling from Japan got louder as a host of officials voiced concern over the dollar's decline and vice finance minister Koichi Hosokawa promised the country would take "bold action" if needed.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone finance ministers are expected to discuss the dollar's fall at a meeting later on Monday, although the head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Jean-Claude Trichet made no mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a speech in Paris.  \par \par \uc2 "The strength of the dollar's downtrend is such that it is hard to bet against it," said Lee Ferridge, head of global market strategy at Rabobank. "My feeling is rhetoric alone will not stop the dollar's fall and we could see a test of $1.35 when New York trade gets into full swing."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at $1.3450 against the euro at 1230 GMT, having fallen to around $1.3460 on Friday after the publication of a disappointing U.S. payrolls report. The greenback traded at 102.32 yen, having fallen on Friday to around 101.83 yen, its lowest since January 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Data on Friday showed the U.S. economy generated only 112,000 new jobs in November, little more than half the consensus forecast.  \par \par \uc2 STRUCTURAL CONCERNS  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has suffered incessant selling in the past two months on renewed worries about the giant U.S. trade and budget deficits and a widespread belief a weaker dollar is needed - and perhaps wanted by Washington - to correct them.  \par \par \uc2 "The payrolls figures suggest the cyclical reasons for buying the dollar are not enough to outweigh the structural reasons for selling," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO.  \par \par \uc2 Data at the weekend suggesting oil-producing countries have already started diversifying reserves out of dollars only highlighted the negative long-term backdrop for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In its quarterly report released on Sunday, the Bank for International Settlements said OPEC countries have cut the share of their deposits in dollars by over 13 percentage points in the last three years, mainly to the euro's advantage.  \par \par \uc2 "The reserve diversification story is a long term negative factor for the dollar," said Adam Myers, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale. "It is feeding into worries over how the U.S. will finance its deficit and the cyclical story is being forgotten."  \par \par \uc2 To be sure, the prospect of a higher U.S. Fed funds rate - which makes dollar deposits more attractive - is providing little support to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll last week found all 20 primary dealers surveyed expected the Fed to raise its key rate by a quarter percentage point to 2.25 percent at its December meeting. Sixteen of the 20 looked for another quarter-point tightening in February.  \par \par \uc2 CENTRAL BANKS EYED  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials in particular have stepped up their warnings in recent days about taking dollar-buying action, calling recent market moves volatile and hinting at possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But traders say the market will keep driving the dollar lower until \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurs. Some believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may ultimately act alone if yen strength accelerates.  \par \par \uc2 Since early October the yen has jumped nearly 9 percent against the dollar, while the euro has surged more than 9 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking on Monday, ECB Governing Council member Axel Weber said short-term moves in exchange rates could cause a shift in competitive relationships and were "highly unwelcome". But he did little to convince the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the euro's strength against the dollar was imminent.  \par \par \uc2 "We have had no concrete signals that the ECB is going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Myers. "People are looking for stronger verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  first."  \par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc fell against both the euro and dollar after Swiss National Bank President Jean-Pierre Roth said weaker economic growth and high oil prices would prompt central banks to shy away from raising interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The market took the comments as an indication Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not raise rates at its next quarterly policy meeting on December 16.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c60080y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
