\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar ticks up, but respite seen temporary.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 07:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 6 (Reuters) - The dollar rose on Monday, back-tracking from record lows hit against the euro on disappointing U.S. jobs data, but traders said it was just a matter of time before the market sells the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.   \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking on the dollar's slide was helping to support the unit against sterling and the Swiss franc, while worries that Japan could step into the market stemmed its fall against the yen.   \par \par \uc2  "While the ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon, the yen's rise should be limited on wariness over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Yoshiyasu Naruse, head of corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at HSBC Ltd.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled across the board on Friday after U.S. non-farm payrolls rose 112,000 in November, well below economists' median forecast for a rise of 180,000.   \par \par \uc2  At 0226 GMT, the dollar was at around 102.10 yen , flat from late U.S. levels on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  In early trade, it fell to a low of 101.91 yen, slightly above a five-year low of 101.83 hit on Thursday, before moving back up partly due to buying by Japanese importers, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly easier at $1.3445 , versus 1.3454 in New York and a record high of 1.3461 marked on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  Sterling stood at around $1.9405  after matching a 12-year peak of 1.9442 earlier in the day.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved up to 1.1317 Swiss francs  after hitting a nine-year low of 1.1301 in U.S. trade.   \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR OUTLOOK DISMAL   \par \par \uc2  Friday's payrolls data also showed the jobless rate was at 5.4 percent, matching forecasts.   \par \par \uc2  "The jobs data brought the market's focus back to the dollar's weakness," said Kikuko Takeda, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.   \par \par \uc2  "I think we should be prepared to see another round of dollar selling," she said, adding that the market would likely target a fall towards 100 yen and a rise in the euro to $1.35.   \par \par \uc2  Despite the weak data, a Reuters poll taken after the figures were released found that all 20 primary dealers surveyed expected the Federal Reserve to raise its key rate by a quarter percentage point to 2.25 percent at its December meeting.   \par \par \uc2  Sixteen of the 20 looked for another quarter-point tightening in February.   \par \par \uc2  "The interest rate outlook isn't a factor for the market," said Takeda at Tokyo-Mitsubishi.   \par \par \uc2  "The jobs data dampened sentiment for the dollar so the market will continue to focus on U.S. deficits."   \par \par \uc2  The dollar also came under pressure on Friday after a German newspaper cited a high-ranking U.S. Treasury official as saying the United States would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  only after the euro reached $1.45.   \par \par \uc2  Most Tokyo traders showed little reaction to the report, saying they were unfamiliar with the newspaper.   \par \par \uc2  They added that it had little effect on the market's view that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the yen rise further.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c60056d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
