\par\par \b \uc2 UK PRESS:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Urging Europe To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2004\par 12:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--A senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said that Japan is urging its European counterparts to join a campaign of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , The Observer newspaper reported.  \par \par \uc2 "If the dollar is depreciating, we should have coordinated action: that has already been communicated to my European counterparts," the unnamed official said.  \par \par \uc2 However, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet made only one passing reference to euro strength after the ECB's policy meeting last Thursday, saying he viewed its rise as "unwelcome."  \par \par \uc2 Trichet declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and urged those who speak about exchange rates to exercise more discipline than they have.  \par \par \uc2 Friday, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterated that the Bush administration has a strong dollar policy.  \par \par \uc2 Snow's comments, made in an interview with CNBC, came as the dollar sat at an all-time low against the euro around $1.3461 and near a four-and-a-half year low against the yen around Y102.05.  \par \par \uc2 In the interview, Snow would not comment on reports that European and Japanese authorities may be considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the dollar's decline.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also warning the White House that there will be "enormous capital flight" from the dollar if the Bush administration maintains its laissez-faire approach to the dollar's decline, The Observer added.  \par \par \uc2 "The Japanese government is going to ask for a strong dollar policy; if it continues to fall, there would be enormous capital flight from the dollar," said Kaoru Yosano, chairman of the LDP's policy council.  \par \par \uc2 Japan will be calling on its fellow G7 governments to demand the U.S. deal with the massive fiscal deficit that has helped prompt the dollar's decline, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Yosano's remarks echoed a warning from the senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, who said that if the U.S. does not push up interest rates to make the dollar more attractive, "the one way sentiment on the dollar will have a negative impact on the flow of capital into the U.S.," the newspaper reported.  \par \par \uc2 -By Neil Keane, Dow Jones Newswires; +44-20-7842-9495; neil.keane@dowjones.com [ 05-12-04 1126GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041205e0c50001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
