\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar builds on gains vs yen ahead of US jobs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2004\par 07:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The dollar edged up against the yen on Friday, building on a rebound from a five-year low ahead of closely watched U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market continued to lock in profits from a round of dollar-selling on Thursday that had also driven the euro to record highs and sterling to a 12-year peak.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a sense of accomplishment in the market after the dollar fell to (those levels)," said Katsunori Kitakura, manager of the treasury department at Chuo Mitsui Trust and Banking.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose as high as 103.56 yen, up from 103.25 in late U.S. trade and well off the five-year low of 101.83 hit on Thursday. By 0308 GMT, it was at around 103.30 .  \par \par \uc2 The euro ticked up to $1.3280 , but it was still down about a cent from the record high of 1.3385.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fetched around 137.25 yen after rising as high as 137.48 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling stood at around $1.9220 , compared with 1.9242 in late New York trade and the 12-year peak of 1.9440.  \par \par \uc2 "It's short-covering ahead of the jobs data. That's what we also saw yesterday," said a trader at a Japanese bank.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. payrolls data for November is due at 1330 GMT. Economists' median forecast is for 180,000 new jobs compared with a rise of 337,000 in October.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the market's reaction to the numbers could serve as a litmus test for the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "I want to see how the market reacts to the jobs data tonight. If the market sells the dollar even if the numbers are good, it'll be a sign that dollar sentiment is still bearish," said Chuo Mitsui's Kitakura.  \par \par \uc2 TIPTOES OVER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Some traders said the dollar was also supported by caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese and European authorities.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Thursday that Japan was in "close contact" with European and U.S. authorities due to the volatile market.  \par \par \uc2 He reiterated on Friday that the recent rise in the yen has been rapid and that Japan would take action if needed.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said on Thursday that recent moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were unwelcome. On \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said that such a weapon exists, but he would "never" comment further on it.  \par \par \uc2 A senior euro zone official said that European finance ministers had not discussed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and had not urged the ECB to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We don't know if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe and will jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but both sets of officials have raised concern about the dollar's fall, so that's making the market nervous," said Kitakura of Chuo Mitsui.  \par \par \uc2 The market showed little reaction to a survey by Japan's Finance Ministry that showed capital spending in July-September rose 14.4 percent from the same quarter last year.  \par \par \uc2 Economists in a Reuters poll had expected a rise of between 8 and 13 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041203e0c3005pq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
