\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises on profit-taking in other  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The dollar rallied across the board on Thursday in a brisk round of profit-taking in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have climbed to highs in recent days.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term traders said they viewed the dollar as oversold, but analysts continued to cite poor underlying sentiment surrounding the long-term negatives weighing on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the wide U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "It's profit-taking," said a sales trader at a Japanese bank in London. "Everyone has got far too short of dollars across the board and it's snowballing now."  \par \par \uc2 Traders remained nervous about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength, but traders said they had not seen any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  insisted on Thursday that its concern about the dollar's steep decline was shared by Europe and the United States, keeping the market guessing about possible concerted action.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking just after the dollar had fallen below 102 yen for the first time since January 2000, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said market moves had been volatile and Japan was in "close contact" with European and U.S. authorities.  \par \par \uc2 Late morning in New York, the euro fell to a session low of $1.3242, down sharply from the record high of $1.3383 reached in overnight trade, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar soared to a session high of 103.40 yen , well off a five-year low of 101.86 yen reached earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc , the dollar was up 1.3 percent at 1.1552 francs.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was down 0.8 percent to $1.9181.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said sterling's relapse was an initial trigger for weakness in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping the dollar firm broadly.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the sell-off in cable (sterling/dollar) precipitated this down move in the euro," said Hugh Walsh, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Fortis Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier, the dollar slipped against the euro after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet reiterated that recent moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were unwelcome but did not use strong enough rhetoric to deter the euro from strengthening, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Trichet was speaking at a news conference after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key interest rate unchanged at 2 percent, as expected.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro is trading close to highs and the market is looking for any indication that the ECB is starting to express more concern," said Steven Englander, chief North American \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Barclays Capital in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "Trichet is not breaking any new ground in expressing current concerns about the euro, so from the point of view of the market, one of the potential factors in blocking euro gains just isn't there," Englander said.  \par \par \uc2 Trichet acknowledged that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a weapon that exists, but said he would "never" comment further on it. He also said the ECB had considered a rate hike, which traders said also helped drive the euro up.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar showed a muted reaction to a report of 349,000 new U.S. jobless claims in the latest week, above economists' forecasts of 330,000.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are paying close attention to U.S. jobs data on the eve of the November non-farm payrolls report, due on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar pared a few losses against the euro after news that U.S. October factory orders, swelled by demand for military aircraft, rose 0.5 percent, exceeding economists' forecasts of a 0.3 percent rise.  \par \par \uc2 (Gertrude Chavez, Jamie McGeever, Kevin Plumberg and Andrea Ricci in New York contributed to this report).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c200970\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
