\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ liquidity projections leave  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt guessing.   \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - A bigger-than-expected surplus in the Bank of Japan's money market projections for Friday has started the market wondering if it could be a sign that Japanese authorities bought dollars for yen on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Most money market traders dismiss the speculation, but it was through such discrepancies that the market first detected the start of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive 15-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in January 2003.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's projections published on Thursday showed that it was expecting a 960 billion yen ($9.35 billion) net surplus in a column headed "Treasury funds and others" - more than 600 billion yen larger than typical forecasts by market watchers.   \par \par \uc2 "It certainly is a bigger surplus than we had estimated," said a money market trader at a Japanese financial institution.   \par \par \uc2 He, as well as others in the market, did not think it was a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that such a possibility could not be 100 percent ruled out.   \par \par \uc2 "December is a month where the government has a lot of payments to the private sector, and the actual supply/demand of funds does often deviate from market forecasts," said Kiyoshi Iida, a senior analyst at Totan Research.   \par \par \uc2 "I suspect it was from a confluence of various factors that the BOJ's surplus projection is exceeding the market's estimates."   \par \par \uc2 The "Treasury funds and others" column includes such items as tax payments to government and the government's payment for goods and services from the private sector, as well transactions with financial institutions.   \par \par \uc2 Because \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions are settled two days after the deals are struck, Friday's surplus would reflect deals done on Wednesday if it were a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Finance Ministry data on Tuesday showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the month to November 26, which meant it had not stepped into the market since mid-March. In the 15 months prior to that, it spent some 35 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been probing its lowest levels against the yen for nearly five years in recent weeks, falling below 102 yen on Thursday for the first time since March 2000. ($1=102.63 Yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c2006y1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
