\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar slides to lows versus euro and yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 07:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The dollar sank to a record low against the euro and fell to its lowest level since March 2000 versus the yen on Thursday as traders played down the chances of joint market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by European and Japanese authorities.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy official, Hiroshi Watanabe, said on Wednesday that "conditions are in place" for Japan and Europe to act jointly to support the dollar and that other countries hurt by the falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could join in for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  But many market players said such action was unlikely and continued selling the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  "The ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is...seen as critical of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Asian central banks," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2  "So it's hard to think that the ECB will jointly act with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the heaviest.   \par \par \uc2  At 0630 GMT, the euro bought around $1.3365, up from $1.3345 in late New York trade and just off the fresh record high of $1.3375 hit earlier in the day.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 102.20 yen after falling to 102.11, a fresh 4 = year low and down nearly half a percent from late trading in New York.   \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $1.9350 per pound, near a 12-year low and close to levels traded just before Britain was ejected from Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism in 1992.   \par \par \uc2  TRICHET IN SPOTLIGHT   \par \par \uc2  Sasaki at JPMorgan said the dollar could slip below 102 yen if ECB chief Jean-Claude Trichet, due to speak following a monetary policy meeting at 1330 GMT, does not back up Watanabe's suggestion of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a higher chance that he will deny it," Sasaki said.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week Trichet indicated that the ECB would keep its policy stance of vigilance against inflation, comments traders viewed as suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to tolerate some euro strength.   \par \par \uc2  A stronger euro lessens the inflationary impact of higher energy costs.   \par \par \uc2  Traders have repeatedly driven the dollar lower despite verbal threats, waiting for evidence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near nine percent drop against the euro and the yen in two months has gone too far too fast for Japanese and European officials.   \par \par \uc2  "Traders are not going to believe it until they see it. They're going to keep blowing up the dollar until actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  happens," said one trader at a European bank.   \par \par \uc2  The market also took little notice of comments from a senior U.S. Treasury official that Washington was commited in cutting its budget deficit to help the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Asked, after a meeting with officials at Bank Indonesia, about U.S. policy regarding the weakening dollar, Assistant Secretary for International Affairs Randal Quarles told reporters: "I explained the commitment to reduce the fiscal deficit as well as to increase U.S. domestic savings." (Additional reporting by Eric Burroughs).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c2004nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
