\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises from new lows in profit-booking binge.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrea Ricci  \par \uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The dollar rallied on Thursday as fears of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp fall in oil prices convinced traders that it was a good time to take profits after days of heavy dollar sales.  \par \par \uc2 After registering another all-time low against the euro overnight, the dollar rose as high as $1.3239 per euro . The dollar had set new lows against the euro in seven of the last eight sessions.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback also rose from a five-year low against the yen and a new 12-year bottom against sterling.  \par \par \uc2 Richard Franulovich, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Banking Corp. in New York, said selling of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the dollar "cascaded" after the dollar made new lows.  \par \par \uc2 Fears about dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the desire to cut back on short dollar positions ahead of Friday's U.S. payrolls report encouraged traders to buy back dollars, Franulovich said.  \par \par \uc2 "People are nervous about the BOJ and there was a big washout of dollar shorts," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Late afternoon in New York, the euro was down 0.43 percent at $1.3272, far below the record high of $1.3383 touched in overnight trade, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was up 0.53 percent at 103.15 yen , well off a five-year low of 101.86 yen reached earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc , the dollar was up 0.94 percent at 1.1510 francs.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was down 0.44 percent to $1.9241 after earlier posting a new 12-year high of $1.9438.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Thursday said market moves had been volatile and Japan was in "close contact" with European and U.S. authorities.  \par \par \uc2 But a senior euro zone official later said that European finance ministers had not discussed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and did not urge the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Comments by an adviser to U.S. President George W. Bush underscored the market's belief that U.S. officials were not as worried about the country's structural imbalances or the weak dollar as their European and Japanese counterparts.  \par \par \uc2 Greg Mankiw, chairman of the president's Council of Economic Advisers, said the U.S. current account gap reflected strong growth and foreign demand for U.S. assets and was not a problem in and of itself.  \par \par \uc2 LOOKING TO U.S. PAYROLLS  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a second day of sharp falls in oil prices also helped boost the dollar on views lower prices would aid the U.S. economy and lessen inflationary pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Oil prices fell nearly 5 percent on Thursday and U.S. light sweet crude prices are now nearly $6 lower than just two days ago at $43.25.  \par \par \uc2 Technical analysts pointed out that the euro, in setting new highs against the dollar during the session and then closing below the prior day's low, had what is called a bearish key reversal day that could portend further losses for the euro and gains for the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But others said dollar gains could be short-lived.  \par \par \uc2 "What we are seeing today is an unwinding of leveraged positions, but many real money names and longer-term model names - any money that has more than a one-week time horizon - are in selling the dollar," said TJ Marta, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with RBC Capital Markets in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. government will release November payrolls data on Friday, and Marta said a strong number could spur further short-term dollar gains. Economists' median forecast is for a rise of 180,000.  \par \par \uc2 "If we happen to get an above-consensus number tomorrow, it perhaps takes the dollar higher," he said. "But the overriding concern with the U.S. economy is structural, and it is hard to make cyclical arguments for the dollar."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c200ci6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
