\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INTERVIEW-Ex-MOF Mizoguchi sees reversal of dollar fall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoko Nishikawa and Shinichi Uchida  \par \uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2004\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The dollar's decline against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is temporary and will reverse as market participants focus on the strength of the U.S. economy, Japan's former top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is moving on market speculation. If players see more strong U.S. data, it is highly possible for a reversal to occur," Mizoguchi, currently head of the Japan Center for International Finance (JCIF), told Reuters in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 He added that such a reversal may have already started as the market has become more nervous about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't get the feeling that the market is pushing the dollar down with strong conviction. Overall, current moves don't appear to be lingering on."  \par \par \uc2 During his term in office as vice finance minister for international affairs, Mizoguchi oversaw a record 35 trillion yen ($340 billion) yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in 2003 and in the first three months of 2004 to help stop the yen's sharp appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 He stepped down in June and later joined the JCIF, a government-affiliated research body.  \par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and is just as likely now to take action if needed.  \par \par \uc2 His successor as vice minister, Hiroshi Watanabe, bore out that view, saying later on Wednesday that Japan and Europe can act together in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in what was one of the clearest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings yet from Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 DEFICIT CONCERNS  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki also said he was ready to take action as needed against unusual moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 In late Tokyo trade, the dollar fetched around 102.75 yen down from 103.08 in late U.S. trade but above Friday's low of 102.15 yen - the lowest rate since March 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi said markets' concerns over the U.S. twin deficits were not well-founded in the light of economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. budget deficit would not to deteriorate to a serious state as Washington has pledged to cut fiscal deficits in coming years, he said, adding that few people believe the U.S. needs to correct its current account deficit through rapid adjustments in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi also said the relative competitiveness of U.S. firms has strengthened since the 1980s and 1990s, when poor profits at companies had combined with the twin deficits to underline the trend of dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "The current movements are temporary... unlike the dollar falls we saw before (in the 1980s and 1990s), he said.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi declined to comment directly on the possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other nations, such as Europe and the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 But he said the stance by the Group of Seven (G7) industrial nations remained unchanged since the statement from its meeting in Boca Raton in February.  \par \par \uc2 In the Boca Raton statement, the G7 said excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates are undesirable for economic growth and they would continue to monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as appropriate. ($1=102.98 Yen) (Additional Reporting by Chikako Mogi).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041201e0c1007q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
