\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: No  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Nov  \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2004\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese finance authorities stayed out of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for most of November, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It was the eighth straight month in which Japanese monetary authorities didn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The MOF said it conducted no yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the period from Oct. 28 to Nov. 26, despite the fact that the dollar reached an almost five-year low versus the yen last week.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback, which was trading above Y106.00 at the end of October, recently dropped to Y102.11, a level not seen since early April 2000. Investors have been selling the dollar across the board on the belief that the U.S. government will tolerate a weaker dollar to help adjust its massive current account and trade deficits. Around 1000 GMT Tuesday, it was trading at Y103.07.  \par \par \uc2 The data confirm the MOF has remained out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since mid-March, when it abruptly ended an unprecedented 15-month yen-selling campaign to keep the buoyant yen from harming Japan's economic recovery by crimping exports.  \par \par \uc2 But market players are growing increasingly wary of the possibility that Japanese authorities may soon resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar continues to slide.  \par \par \uc2 Top Japanese officials have regularly warned that the government will take action if it feels that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are too disruptive or are straying too far from economic fundamentals  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covers trades which settle in November. Spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 30-11-04 1016GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041130e0bu000i0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
