\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in Nov.  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2004\par 11:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November, despite the rapid appreciation of the yen against the dollar this month.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF's data showed the ministry stayed away from the markets from Oct. 28 to Nov. 26, debunking speculation among some traders that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise against the dollar recently.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a four-and-a-half-year low of 102.15 yen on Friday, threatening to break below the psychologically important 100 yen mark, amid worries the U.S. economy may be having trouble financing its yawning current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced back this week to around 103 yen largely due to position adjustments ahead of U.S. payrolls data later in the week.  \par \par \uc2 The last time the MOF stepped into the market was on March 16, when the dollar fell close to 2 yen on the day to around 108.60 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities spent 35 trillion yen ($340.2 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through 2003 to March 2004 in an effort to secure its export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Compared to that period, the dollar is trading at much lower levels but traders think Tokyo is more tolerant about the dollar's fall versus the yen as the economy seems to be on a firmer footing.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the yen has not risen against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the euro, alleviating the pain for Japanese exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Still, Finance Ministry officials have repeated in recent weeks that they are ready to act if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Tuesday the yen's recent rise was rapid and that authorities were on the alert.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders expect Tokyo to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar falls below 100 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Others think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely in the near future because the yen has not strengthened against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unlike earlier this year when the yen rose broadly due to foreign investors' buying of Japanese shares. ($1=102.87 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041130e0bu006tf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
