\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms tentatively as focus turns to US data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comments, changes byline and dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The dollar gained tentatively on Monday, recovering from last week's record low against the euro and a 4-1/2-year trough against the yen as traders turned their sights to U.S. economic reports due later in the week.  \par \par \uc2 Signs that China is in no rush to let its pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate against the dollar helped lend some support to the greenback, which has fallen for 10 consecutive weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao on Sunday played down the likelihood of a near-term yuan revaluation and questioned why the United States had not acted to stem the dollar's fall.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's respite on Monday was also aided in part by technical factors as some players viewed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prolonged fall as overdone for the moment, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Tim O'Sullivan, trading manager with Gain Capital in Warren, New Jersey said the market's main focus would be on data to be released towards the end of the week, particularly the November U.S. payrolls report on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Economists foresee on average a rise of 180,000 in non-farm jobs and the jobless rate declining to 5.4 percent from 5.5.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the dollar's recent inability to rally convincingly on strong data, if the jobs report were robust, market positioning might play in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's favor, he surmised.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is getting aggressively short of dollars.... At this point I don't see (the dollar) shrugging off this type of economic data," O'Sullivan added.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists were also waiting for Tuesday's release of Chicago area manufacturing data and Wednesday's Institute for Supply Management figures on national manufacturing for any clues on dollar direction.  \par \par \uc2 By mid-morning in New York, the euro slipped to around $1.3253 according to Reuters data, down about 0.3 percent from levels late on Friday and off its record high attained Friday around $1.3329.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar rose 0.2 percent to 102.75 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc came under pressure after the chairman of the Swiss National Bank signaled the bank may be reluctant to raise interest rates for a third time this year next month.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar rose 0.5 percent to 1.1446 francs.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling slipped 0.3 percent to $1.8887.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet renewed warnings against a stronger euro, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent movements were not welcome. The ECB holds a policy setting meeting on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the dollar's gains on Monday were only a pause in its long-term downtrend and were driven in part by technical factors.  \par \par \uc2 "We set a new high (in euro/dollar) on Friday and the market is a bit exhausted and overdone," said Peter Fontaine, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at KBC in Brussels.  \par \par \uc2 "But everybody is still very negative on the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled to a record low against the euro, and multi-year lows against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after a report that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had cut back on U.S. Treasuries in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adviser quoted in the report later said he had no knowledge of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions and the dollar pulled up from its lows.  \par \par \uc2 But the report played on one of the market's biggest fears - that without purchases of dollar assets by central banks, the United States may find it difficult or even impossible to finance its large current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Data showing a big decline in Japanese retail sales in October had little impact as market players watched for any signs the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preparing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen's export-damaging rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's vice finance minister Koichi Hosokawa repeated his warnings against the yen's recent rise, saying authorities would act on rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. (Additional reporting by Justyna Pawlak in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt00anq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
