\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pauses after recent losses, still near lows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The dollar held above last week's record low against the euro and 4-1/2 year low against the yen on Monday, winning some respite after 10 consecutive weeks of losses.   \par \par \uc2  Signs that China is in no rush to let its pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate against the dollar gave some support to the greenback which has shed nearly 9 percent against the euro and the yen in the last two months.   \par \par \uc2  Speaking on Sunday, Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao played down the likelihood of a near-term yuan revaluation and questioned why the United States had taken no action to stem the dollar's fall.   \par \par \uc2  In Europe, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet renewed warnings against a stronger euro, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent movements were not welcome.   \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing a bit of corrective activity in the dollar, but I would not expect it to get very far or last very wrong," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in London.   \par \par \uc2  "There is a slight bit of nervousness edging into the market after comments from global policymakers."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was up 0.3 percent on the day at 102.86 yen  and 0.2 percent\par up at $1.3260 per euro        in European trade.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WHO'S STILL BUYING?\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled to a record low against the euro, at $1.3329,\par and multi-year lows against most major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday after a\par report that China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had cut back on U.S. Treasuries in its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser quoted in the report later said he had no\par knowledge of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions and the dollar pulled up from its\par lows.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the report played on one of the market's biggest fears - that\par without purchases of dollar assets by central banks, the United States\par may find it difficult or even impossible to finance its large current\par account deficit.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The comments from China have given the dollar some support against\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the bear trend is very much in place," said Paul\par Mackel, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN AMRO.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Everyone is focused on central banks. Any hint they are changing the\par composition of their reserves could put renewed pressure on the\par dollar," said Mackel.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese data showing a big decline in retail sales in October had\par little market impact. Instead, market players are keeping an eye out\par for signs that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is preparing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the\par yen's export-damaging rise against the dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's vice finance minister Koichi Hosokawa repeated his warnings\par against the yen's recent rise, saying authorities would act on rapid\par moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UBS analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a "big worry", but that the yen's\par gains had been mostly fuelled by speculative bets rather than\par investment flows into Japan, potentially limiting any further\par appreciation.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SWISS PRESSURE\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Swiss franc came under pressure after the chairman of the Swiss\par National Bank (SNB) signalled the bank may be reluctant to raise\par interest rates for a third time this year next month.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market developments show that in highly\par turbulent times the Swiss franc can come under upward speculative\par pressure," SNB chief Jean-Pierre Roth said in a speech prepared for\par delivery at the 50th anniversary of the Bank of Israel in Jerusalem.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This may interfere with our domestic monetary strategy," he added.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt009kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
