\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar stuck near lows, central banks eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chikako Mogi  \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 08:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The dollar stayed in sight of a record low against the euro and a 4-1/2-year low versus the yen on Monday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained vulnerable to worries about major central banks trimming dollar assets.  \par \par \uc2 But profit-taking on short positions gave a small lift to the dollar, which has shed nearly 9 percent against the euro and the yen in two months. Market players also kept an eye out for potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders said it was only a matter of time before dollar selling resumed, although participants could loosen their grip somewhat ahead of key U.S. jobs data due on Friday. "The market took a break from its recent fast-pitched move, which was precipitated by market rumours," said a trader at a large Japanese securities firm.  \par \par \uc2 "After the dollar hit a new low versus the euro and fell as far as 102.15 yen last week, it was time for position adjustments."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's latest woes came on Friday from a report, later denied, that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had cut back on U.S. Treasuries in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 That heighten one of the market's biggest fears - that Asian central banks may stop helping to fund a record U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 A JPMorgan Chase Bank report said that fund inflows were still dwindling while foreign central banks were not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much as before.  \par \par \uc2 As the value of U.S. assets remains relatively expensive, the dollar must depreciate more to make those assets cheaper in order to entice fund flows back into the United States, the report said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0700 GMT, the dollar bought around 102.90 yen , up from Friday's 102.15 yen, the lowest level since March 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar had traded as high as 103.45 yen on Friday before resuming its downward slide.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed in a range against the single European unit, trading at around 136.40 yen per euro .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar pared earlier gains to trade at around $1.3260 per euro . It was still up from $1.3296 in late New York trade on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 It hit a record low of $1.3330 on Friday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister, Sadakazu Tanigaki, repeated on Monday his warning that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements needed to be watched closely and that Japan would take decisive action when needed.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at UBS Investment Bank said in a note to clients that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a "big worry", but that the yen's gains had been mostly fuelled by speculative bets rather than investment flows into Japan, potentially limiting any further appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Others, such as Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said that current dollar/yen levels were worrying for Japan as the market shows no sign of quickly turning around.  \par \par \uc2 But Takashima said it would be difficult for Japan to reverse market trends alone, and that it would take time for it to agree with other major central banks on coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "At current market levels, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could happen anytime, but external factors suggest preparations are still some way off," he said.  \par \par \uc2 He added that euro-zone officials seemed to be tolerating current levels for the euro as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength helped to curb inflationary pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, speculation that China may soon loosen the peg of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar and let it appreciate helped to fuel dollar losses against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Such speculation has mounted ahead of an upcoming meeting of top Chinese economic officials.  \par \par \uc2 But Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao played down the likelihood of a yuan revaluation in the near term, saying over the weekend that China needed a stable economy and healthy financial system to unshackle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg. (Additional reporting by Eric Burroughs).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt006sn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
