r Corp (7203.T) to invest in\par and back the restructuring of the troubled home builder.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Australian steelmaker OneSteel (OST.AX) missed out on global steel\par sector euphoria, slipping 3.8 percent on news of production problems at\par a blast furnace, but Australian retail stocks were up on hopes for\par bumper Christmas sales. The S&P ASX 200  touched another record high at\par 3.933.3 before closing up 0.4 percent at 3,926.8.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong's Hang Seng  was up 1.42 percent at 14,092.86 with Hutchison\par Whampoa Ltd. (0013.HK) a top gainer, rising 4.2 percent on talk that\par its partly owned Canadian oil unit, Husky Energy          , may be sold\par to a Chinese oil firm.\par Singapore's Straits Times  climbed 0.62 percent, Taiwan's benchmark\par index         added 0.11 percent and South Korea's KOSPI         rose\par 0.85 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World stocks as measured by the MSCI  were up 0.14 percent, just below\par a 3-year high.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December 10-year JGB futures  slipped 0.25 points to 138.55 in reaction\par to the stock market's climb and on caution ahead of a 1.9 trillion yen\par auction of 10-year JGBs on Thursday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Standard & Poor's 500 Index  put on 0.08 percent to 1,182.65 and\par the Nasdaq Composite Index         edged 0.03 percent lower to\par 2,101.97.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt00692\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
