\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar knocked to record low vs euro, punches back.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2004\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a record low against the euro for a fourth day running on Friday on jitters about a drop in China's dollar reserves but rebounded sharply as traders grew nervous about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit tumbled to beyond $1.33 per euro and 4-1/2 year lows near 102 yen in Asia but jumped in European trade as doubts about an earlier report on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves helped trigger a pullback.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were also nervous about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by either the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Bank of Japan to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, since worries about the U.S. current account deficit have knocked nearly nine percent off the greenback against the euro and the yen since early October.  \par \par \uc2 "It's been incredible price action," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "The private sector has already thrown in the towel on the dollar, and now you are getting more and more signs that central banks are doing so. Then we had a push higher in dollar/yen which people were wondering might be the BoJ, but it didn't look like it."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a record low against the euro of around $1.3329 in Asian trade but roared to $1.3185 in European trade.  \par \par \uc2 It was at $1.3254 per euro at 1250 GMT, steady from levels late on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a 4-1/2 year low of 102.18 yen, recovered to 103.40, and was at 102.87 yen at 1250 GMT, up a third of a percent from late Thursday levels.  \par \par \uc2 The pound hit a nine-month high of $1.9040 in Asia, within sight of 12-year highs, but then lost as much as two cents at one point in Europe.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also recovered in Europe from nine-year lows against an index of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Swiss franc, 12-year lows against the Canadian dollar and 16-year lows against the New Zealand dollar set in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 A partial holiday in the United States following Thanksgiving on Thursday kept markets on their toes, as central banks are notorious for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin markets.  \par \par \uc2 CHINA STIRS, DOLLAR FRIES  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was burnt in Asia after a Chinese newspaper quoted a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee as saying the country had trimmed its U.S. Treasury holdings in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, trying to minimise losses from a falling dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback bounced back after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adviser quoted by the paper later said that he had no knowledge of any government action on China's reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Markets have recently been sensitive to speculation that central banks are reducing the share of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves denominated in dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The sharpness of the move raised short-lived queries among traders as to whether there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "It was just an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spoof," said a senior trader at a London-based bank."  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that China could soon revalue its pegged yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and let it strengthen against the dollar has also captivated market attention, especially ahead of an annual meeting of China's top economic officials in Beijing over the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 China has come under intense pressure to revalue the yuan, which is pegged near 8.28 to the dollar. Countries like the United States have complained that the rate is too low, making Chinese exports unfairly cheap.  \par \par \uc2 Any revaluation of the yuan would boost other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Friday Japanese authorities would take action as needed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if exchange rates moved too rapidly.  \par \par \uc2 "These comments are significant, coming from the Finance Minister," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan will probably try and defend the (dollar/yen) 101.20 1999 low, and certainly the 100 level."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to weaken the yen in the first quarter.  \par \par \uc2 In a light calendar on Friday, ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet speaks in Rio de Janeiro at 1805 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041126e0bq009vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
