\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits record low vs euro, then fights back.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2004\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a record low against the euro for a fourth day running on Friday but rebounded swiftly as traders grew nervous about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rallied nearly 1-1/2 cents from record lows against the euro and recovered from earlier 4-1/2 year lows against the yen, as doubts about an earlier report on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves helped trigger a pullback in European trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders are nervous about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by either the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Bank of Japan to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, after worries about the U.S. current account deficit knocked nearly nine percent off the greenback against the euro and the yen since early October.  \par \par \uc2 "There are considerable nerves in the market," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London.  \par \par \uc2 "These moves do suggest the market is twitchy about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a record low against the euro of around $1.3329 in Asian trade but roared to $1.3185 in European trade.  \par \par \uc2 It was at $1.3210 per euro at 1100 GMT, up a quarter percent from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a 4-1/2 year low of 102.18 yen , recovered to 103.42, and was at 103 yen at 1100 GMT, half a percent up from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The pound hit a nine-month high of $1.9040 in Asia, within sight of 12-year highs, but then lost as much as two cents at one point in Europe.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar also recovered in Europe from nine-year lows against an\par index of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   and the Swiss franc       , 12-year lows against\par the Canadian dollar        and 16-year lows against the New Zealand\par dollar        set in Asia.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A partial holiday in the United States following Thanksgiving on Thursday kept markets on their toes, with central banks notorious for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in thin markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CHINA CONFUSION  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar crumbled in Asia after a Chinese newspaper quoted a member of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy committee as saying the country had trimmed its U.S. Treasury holdings in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, trying to minimise losses from a falling dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the greenback bounced back after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser quoted by the paper later said that he had no knowledge about China's reserves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The sharpness of the move raised short-lived queries among traders as to whether there was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It was just an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spoof," said a senior trader at a London-based bank."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculation that China could soon revalue its pegged yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and let it strengthen against the dollar has also captivated market attention, especially ahead of an annual meeting of China's top economic officials in Beijing over the weekend.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has come under intense pressure to revalue the yuan, which is pegged near 8.28 to the dollar. Countries like the United States have complained that the rate is too low, making Chinese exports unfairly cheap.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any revaluation of the yuan would boost other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Japanese authorities would take action as needed in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if exchange rates moved too rapidly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "These comments are significant, coming from the Finance Minister," said Halpenny.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan will probably try and defend the (dollar/yen) 101.20 1999 low, and certainly the 100 level."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily to weaken the yen in the first quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a light calendar on Friday, ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet speaks in Rio de Janeiro at 1805 GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041126e0bq008vi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
