\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Asia Business News at 0540 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2004\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Editor: Andrew Callus\par     Telephone: +65 6870 3852\par     All times GMT.\par     TOP STORIES:\par     TOKYO - Dollar slides to new low against euro\par     TOKYO/SEOUL - Carmaker steel shortage favours steel firms\par  SEOUL - S.Korea LCD plants delayed by Canon problems\par     TOKYO - Japan consumer prices fall suggests no rate hike\par     TOKYO - Steel shortages threaten to cap Japan output\par     SINGAPORE - Singapore factory output triple expectations\par     - - - -\par     COMPANIES\par     TOKYO/SEOUL - Asian steel makers will have the upper hand\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in future price negotiations as Japanese car makers face a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 serious shortage, signalling a further rise in steel prices and   \par \par \uc2 slimmer earnings for the auto industry (MINERALS-STEEL-AUTO   \par \par \uc2 (WRAPUP 1), expect by 0930, by Chang-Ran Kim and Rhee So-eu,   \par \par \uc2 800 words)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL - The world's top two makers of liquid crystal   \par \par \uc2 displays (LCD), Samsung Electronics and LG.Philips LCD, face   \par \par \uc2 production delays because of problems with Canon Inc. equipment   \par \par \uc2 (TECH-LCD (UPDATE 3), expect by 0600, by Jean Yoon, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL - Unionised workers at South Korea's top car maker   \par \par \uc2 Hyundai Motor launch a full strike, taking the lead in labour   \par \par \uc2 action against proposed new labour laws (AUTOS-KOREA-STRIKE   \par \par \uc2 (UPDATE 1), by Kim Kyoung-wha, with desk, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL - South Korea's Samsung and LG, already challenging   \par \par \uc2 top handset maker Nokia in the world's biggest markets, are   \par \par \uc2 taking the fight to fast-growing India (TELECOMS-INDIA-KOREA   \par \par \uc2 (ANALYSIS), moved at 0326, by Jean Yoon and Shailendra   \par \par \uc2 Bhatnagar, 890 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - First-half results from Japan's big life insurers   \par \par \uc2 are expected to show a modest improvement in their financial   \par \par \uc2 health, but the sector remains under pressure from meagre   \par \par \uc2 investment returns (FINANCIAL-JAPAN (WRAPUP 1), expect by 0900,   \par \par \uc2 by David McMahon, 700 words)   \par \par \uc2 NINGBO, China - China's Ningbo, the country's busiest port   \par \par \uc2 after Shanghai, will sign agreements in January with a trio of   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong firms to spend $1.05 billion building eight to nine   \par \par \uc2 new berths (TRANSPORT-CHINA-NINGBO (UPDATE 2), expect by 0700,   \par \par \uc2 by Benjamin Kang Lim, 550 words)    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     MARKETS/ECONOMY\par     TOKYO - The dollar hits a record low against the euro and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its lowest in nearly five years against the yen, as the Bank of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 England says its fall may continue and speculation swirls that   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may cut its U.S. bond holdings (MARKETS-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (UPDATE 1),   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expect by 0700, by Eric Burroughs, 600 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See also MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 2)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO - Japanese consumer prices fall slightly in October   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from a year earlier, underscoring expectations there will be no   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 immediate change to the Bank of Japan's super-loose monetary   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy (ECONOMY-JAPAN (UPDATE 3), expect by 0700, by Yoko   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nishikawa, 700 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO - Steel shortages are threatening to cap industrial   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 output in Japan, but economists say a huge downturn in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 production is unlikely as long as demand for goods such as cars   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 remains strong. (ECONOMY-JAPAN-OUTPUT, expect by 0700, by Chisa   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fujioka, 500 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE - Singapore's factory output rises 5.1 percent in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October from September, more than triple market expectations,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 putting the economy on track to meet a 2004 growth forecast,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government data shows (ECONOMY-SINGAPORE-MANUFACTURING (UPDATE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1), moved 0526, 450 words, by Jacqueline Wong)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See also ECONOMY-SINGAPORE (ANALYSIS), moved at 0100   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO - Japan seems to have completed its massive buying of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasuries for now, with officials comfortable with the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ratio of securities to deposits in foreign reserves that have   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 been bloated by aggressive yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until March   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (ECONOMY-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -RESERVES, expect by 0800, by Yoko Nishikawa, 700   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG - Hong Kong is expected to report economic growth   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slowed between the second and third quarters of this year as   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exports started to cool and consumers grew more cautious about   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 spending. (ECONOMY-HONGKONG-GDP (UPDATE 1), expect by 0915, by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Susan Fenton, 600 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL - South Korea's current account surplus more than   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 triples during the first 10 months, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data shows,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 adding to upward pressure on the won \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  already at   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seven-year highs against the dollar. (ECONOMY-KOREA (UPDATE 2),   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expect by 0700, by Oh Jung-hwa, 500 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG - The explosion in Hong Kong's market for   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 low-risk notes linked to stocks and bonds has led to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overcompetition and is forcing banks to start targeting   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore and Taiwan for growth (FINANCIAL-ASIA-STRUCTURED,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 moved at 0510, by Brian Kelleher, 800 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041126e0bq0059a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
