\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar selling gathers pace, euro at new record high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 24 (Reuters) - The dollar crashed to a record low versus the euro on Wednesday as sales of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against most of its major competitors gathered momentum.  \par \par \uc2 Some investors accelerated their selling following news that Russia may review the share of euros in its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, while others used higher oil prices as a sell signal.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, there were few signs that the world's policymakers were likely to prop up the dollar and the market continued to worry about the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "Sentiment is extremely bearish," said Stephen Jen, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in London.  \par \par \uc2 "We are in an overshooting territory and this is going to continue unless it's stopped by the authorities. The key driver has been a shift in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 By 1100 GMT, the dollar fell to $1.3167 per euro, a new record low and down half a percent from late New York levels. The dollar also slumped to a nine-year low of 1.1500 Swiss francs.  \par \par \uc2 It stood at 102.95 yen, down from 103.30 in New York and within sight of a four-year low of around 102.70 hit on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Oil prices have crept up since last week, reversing their decline since late October, with U.S. light crude futures briefly rising above $50 per barrel on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 ONLY BAD NEWS  \par \par \uc2 The market's negative sentiment towards the dollar was cemented last week after the Group of 20 rich and developing nations gave no indication they would take action to stem the dollar's fall at a high profile meeting in Berlin.  \par \par \uc2 Instead, policymakers from the U.S., Europe and Japan continued to blame each other for the dollar's woes.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. also appeared to accept the downtrend, which has taken the dollar to a nine-year low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 And U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan aggravated worries over the current account deficit when he said last week that market appetite for U.S. assets will eventually dwindle, raising the prospect that inflows of foreign funds into the U.S. will become insufficient to offset its wide current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Russia added to dollar-negative news, when the first deputy chairman of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Alexei Ulyukayev, said on Tuesday the bank was reviewing its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves "with the highest priority".  \par \par \uc2 Speculation swirled in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could further increase the share of euros in its $100 billion-plus reserves. Euros already account for 25-30 percent of the reserves, compared with 10 percent two years ago.  \par \par \uc2 "The comments from Russia yesterday - that's a big thing for sentiment right now," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO. "Any story that the market can put a dollar negative spin on is welcomed."  \par \par \uc2 PATIENCE SNAPS?  \par \par \uc2 However, investors were also wary of any signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or Europe, could lose patience and try to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has formed a consensus that $1.35 (per euro) is a danger zone in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...The ECB won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  below $1.35. But at some point they have to consider unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Morgan Stanley's Jen.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry kept up its campaign of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, with a senior official chiding the market for allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to fluctuate too rapidly and ignoring fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 However, a senior official from Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party said the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be fleeting and minimal in light of the overall volume of trade.  \par \par \uc2 "They may step up to smooth things over as they don't want things to get too disorderly but, that said, it's just going to slow the yen's uptrend not prevent it," ABN AMRO's Mackel said.  \par \par \uc2 On the data calendar, the U.S. Commerce Department releases October durable goods orders data at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Economists in a Reuters survey expect a median 0.5 percent rise in October orders, compared with a rise of 0.2 percent in the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 The University of Michigan releases the final November consumer sentiment index at 1445 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters expect a reading of 96.0 compared with 91.7 in the final October report.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041124e0bo007by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
