\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar plumbs new all-time low against euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Hunt  \par \uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 10:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 24 (Reuters) - The dollar plumbed a record low against the euro on Wednesday, as news that Russia may consider boosting the share of euros in its vast foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves gave traders another reason to dump the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Higher oil prices also hurt the greenback and a warning issued last week by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan about further dollar weakness continued to resonate throughout the market.  \par \par \uc2 "The comments from Russia yesterday - that's a big thing for sentiment right now," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO. "Any story that the market can put a dollar negative spin on is welcomed."  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan warned that the U.S. deficits were unsustainable and that investor appetite for dollars was bound to dwindle.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0850 GMT, the dollar had fallen to $1.3129 per euro, new record low and down a third of a percent from late New York levels. The dollar also slumped to near a nine-year low of 1.1543 Swiss francs.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at 103.05 yen down from 103.30 in New York and within sight of a four-year low of around 102.70 hit on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 FRESH SELLING  \par \par \uc2 The dollar met with fresh selling in New York on Tuesday when the first deputy chairman of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Alexei Ulyukayev, said that the bank was reviewing its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves "with the highest priority".  \par \par \uc2 Speculation swirled in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could further increase the share of euros in its $100 billion-plus reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Euros already account for 25-30 percent of the reserves, compared with 10 percent two years ago.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were more hesitant about buying the yen, due in part to worries that a further rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could prompt the Japanese authorities to restart yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry kept up its campaign of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, with a senior official chiding the market for allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to fluctuate too rapidly and ignoring fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 However, a senior official from Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party said the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be fleeting and minimal in light of the overall volume of trade.  \par \par \uc2 "They may step up to smooth things over as they don't want things to get too disorderly but, that said, it's just going to slow the yen's uptrend not prevent it," ABN AMRO's Mackel said. "The message is mixed at the moment."  \par \par \uc2 A recent rebound in oil prices also helped to weaken the dollar, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Oil prices have crept up since late last week, reversing their decline since late October, with U.S. light crude futures briefly rising above $50 per barrel on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 On the data calendar, the U.S. Commerce Department releases October durable goods orders data at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Economists in a Reuters survey expect a median 0.5 percent rise in October orders, compared with a rise of 0.2 percent in the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 The University of Michigan releases the final November consumer sentiment index at 1445 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters expect a reading of 96.0 compared with 91.7 in the final October report.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041124e0bo0079l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
